<p>This page explains what Zymplo keeps and how to ask us to delete it. There is a dedicated section for what arrives from <a href="#instagram">Instagram</a> and from <a href="#facebook">Facebook</a>.</p>

<h2>What we keep</h2>
<p>Zymplo helps you organise your work from WhatsApp. We keep:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your WhatsApp number and your name.</li>
  <li>The messages you exchange with the bot.</li>
  <li>What you write down: customers, payments due, expenses, appointments and notes.</li>
  <li>The tax receipts (NFS-e) you issue in Brazil.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="instagram">Instagram · what we keep if you connect your account</h2>
<p>Connecting Instagram is optional. If you connect it, we keep:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your Instagram account identifier and your public username.</li>
  <li>The permissions you granted when connecting.</li>
  <li>An access key, stored encrypted, and its expiry date.</li>
  <li>The direct messages people send you: the text, the name or identifier of the sender, and the full notification Meta sends us.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not keep your profile picture, your posts or your follower list.</p>

<h2 id="facebook">Facebook · what we keep if you connect your Page</h2>
<p>Connecting Facebook is optional. If you connect it, we keep:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your Facebook Page identifier and its public name.</li>
  <li>The permissions you granted when connecting.</li>
  <li>An access key, stored encrypted, and its expiry date.</li>
  <li>The Messenger messages people send you: the text, the name or identifier of the sender, and the full notification Meta sends us.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not keep your profile picture, your posts or your friend list.</p>

<h2>How to request deletion</h2>

<h3>Option 1 · By email (works for everything, including Instagram and Facebook)</h3>
<div class="step">
  <p><span class="step-num">1</span> Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@zymplo.com">privacy@zymplo.com</a> with the subject <strong>"Data deletion"</strong>.</p>
  <p><span class="step-num">2</span> Tell us what you want deleted: everything, or only what came from Instagram or Facebook.</p>
  <p><span class="step-num">3</span> Include your Zymplo WhatsApp number and, if it applies, your Instagram username or your Facebook Page name.</p>
  <p>We delete the connection (identifier, public name, permissions and access key) and the messages received through that channel.</p>
</div>

<h3>Option 2 · From the app (deletes your Zymplo account)</h3>
<div class="step">
  <p><span class="step-num">1</span> Open the Zymplo app and go to <strong>Profile</strong>.</p>
  <p><span class="step-num">2</span> Tap <strong>Delete my account</strong> and confirm.</p>
</div>
<div class="box-warning">
  <strong>Heads up:</strong> today, deleting from the app does not reach the Instagram or Facebook connection, nor the messages that arrived through it. To delete those, ask by email (option 1): we do it by hand and confirm it to you.
</div>

<h3>Also · cut off access from Meta</h3>
<div class="box">
  <p><strong>Instagram:</strong> open Instagram → Settings → Websites and apps → remove Zymplo.</p>
  <p><strong>Facebook:</strong> open Facebook → Settings &amp; privacy → Settings → Apps and websites → remove Zymplo.</p>
  <p>This immediately stops new messages reaching Zymplo. On its own it does not delete what was already stored: for that, use the request above.</p>
</div>

<h2>How long it takes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>We confirm your request within <strong>15 business days</strong> (LGPD · GDPR).</li>
  <li>The deletion is completed within <strong>30 days</strong> of your request.</li>
  <li>Encrypted backups are destroyed 30 days after the deletion.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What stays, and for how long</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Tax receipts (NFS-e) issued in Brazil:</strong> 5 years, by tax law. We cannot delete them. They stay linked to an anonymous identifier.</li>
  <li><strong>Anonymised technical logs:</strong> 90 days, for security and fraud prevention.</li>
  <li><strong>Encrypted backups:</strong> 30 days after the deletion.</li>
</ul>

<div class="box-warning">
  <strong>This cannot be undone.</strong> Once the deletion is done we cannot recover your data. If you want a copy, ask us for an export by email first.
</div>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@zymplo.com">privacy@zymplo.com</a>.</p>

